  "kind": "thrown_save",
  "exercises": "The record of good/lease_after_refused_commit.json. Frame 3's commit writes alt_cells#1 and then its record save throws. A throw that carries a status (encoded's 413, _capacity's 507 or 503) comes before the record is written: the instance keeps serving, the lists are as they were, and alt_cells#1 is an orphan the next lease never reads. A throw without a status can come after the rename, so the record may have landed: the outcome is unknown. _open sets the instance's failure, so it serves nothing more, its lists included, until a restart; the restart's first lock entry reconciles, and its full read rebuilds every list from the durable heads. If the save landed, the durable head is alt_cells#1 and the rebuilt list holds it; if not, the head is alt_cells#0 and alt_cells#1 stays an orphan. Neither reconciliation saves a verified head, and no list is ever extended by the commit that threw.",
